    <li><b><a href="#fn_2" target="_blank">^</a></b> In LSL the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Key" target="_blank">key</a> type is implemented as a <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/String" target="_blank">string</a> (but with different operators and restrictions). <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Typecast" target="_blank">Typecasting</a> between string and key types has no effect on the data contained.</li>
    <li><b><a href="#fn_3" target="_blank">^</a></b> There are four ways for a script to target itself: by <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetLinkNumber" target="_blank">precise link number</a>, <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LINK_THIS" target="_blank">LINK_THIS</a>, <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LINK_SET" target="_blank">LINK_SET</a> and <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LINK_ALL_CHILDREN" target="_blank">LINK_ALL_CHILDREN</a> (if the prim is a child prim).</li>
  </ul>
